1h1. unshield / explode, MIT (linked dependency + test fixtures)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

crates/exav-unpack/src/formats/ishield_z.rs reads InstallShield `.z` archives
through the `unshield` crate, whose only real dependency is `explode`, a leaf
decoder for the PKWARE Data Compression Library "implode" codec those archives
use. Both MIT.

The fixtures in crates/exav-unpack/tests/fixtures/ishieldz/ are that project's
own examples, redistributed under the same terms. `undhr.z` is shipped alongside
`undhr.md`, the uncompressed original, which is what lets the decoder be checked
against the real file rather than against itself.

This is a DIFFERENT format from the InstallShield `ISc(` InstallScript cabinet,
whose only implementation is the LGPL `unshield` C project (never read), and the
reason that format stays recognised-but-unopened.

Upstream: https://github.com/agrif/unshield , https://github.com/agrif/explode
Copyright (c) Aaron Griffith.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1h2. iced-x86, MIT (generated opcode tables)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

crates/exav-x86/src/generated.rs holds the SIMD, system and VEX regions of the
x86 opcode maps. It is not hand-written and not transcribed from a manual: it is
emitted by crates/exav-x86/tools/gen-tables, which decodes a probe for every
(prefix, opcode, /digit, mod) combination with `iced-x86` and records what came
back. The tables are therefore derived from `iced-x86`'s data, and the MIT
License requires retaining its copyright and permission notice (the MIT text is
in the exav LICENSE file).

`iced-x86` is also the oracle that exav-x86's differential tests and the
`x86_decode` fuzz target compare against, including the decoding that
exav-pe-emu drives. It is a dev-dependency only: the decoder exav-pe-emu uses at
run time is exav-x86, and no iced code reaches a shipped artifact.

Upstream: https://github.com/icedland/iced
Copyright (C) 2018-present iced project and contributors.


