adapted from the `bzip2-rs` crate (version 0.1.2): the streaming decoder buffers
enough input for the largest compressed block (upstream buffered only the
uncompressed block size, which a block of incompressible data exceeds), the
MSRV and nightly code paths are collapsed, and the doc examples that need the
upstream test files are removed. Dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0; the MIT or
Apache terms apply at the distributor's choice.

Upstream: https://github.com/paolobarbolini/bzip2-rs
