Format documentation consulted
-----------------------------

Some decoders were written from format descriptions rather than from any code.
Recorded here because a decoder's provenance is part of what makes it auditable:

  EGG        ESTsoft Corp., "EGG Format Specification, Version 1.0", the
             vendor's own published document. No ESTsoft code was used.

  AZO        ESTsoft's own compression algorithm, absent from the EGG spec.
             `crates/exav-unpack/src/formats/azo.rs` and `azo_tables.rs` are a
             Rust port of the AZO decoder in `EggDotNet`
             (https://github.com/akolman/EggDotNet), MIT, Copyright (c) Andrew
             Kolman. ESTsoft's own UnEgg library was NOT used: its licence
             forbids commercial use without approval and forbids using it to
             develop a compression algorithm.

  HWP3       Preamble offsets taken from `java-hwp`
             (https://github.com/ddoleye/java-hwp), Apache-2.0.
             Copyright the java-hwp authors. Validated against
             `testHWP_3.0.hwp` from the Apache Tika test corpus
             (https://github.com/apache/tika), Apache-2.0, Copyright the
             Apache Software Foundation, vendored as
             `crates/exav-unpack/tests/fixtures/hwp3/tika_testHWP_3.0.hwp`.

  ALZ        Structure cross-checked against `unalz` (zlib license) and
             `unar`, used as external oracles rather than as sources.

The exav LICENSE file contains the MIT text, and section 4 the Apache License
2.0.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Build-only tooling
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything above concerns code that reaches a shipped artifact. The
documentation site under `www/` builds with an npm toolchain whose lockfile
includes packages under stronger terms, LGPL-3.0-or-later among them. None of it
is linked into, bundled with, or distributed alongside any exav binary, crate or
WASM module: it runs at build time to produce static HTML and is listed here so
that a licence scan of the repository has an answer rather than a finding.


